Title: filetime: set AROS ABIv1 mtime through utimes
Base: crates.io filetime 0.2.29 SHA-256 5c287a33c7f0a620c38e641e7f60827713987b3c0f26e8ddc9462cc69cf75759
Date: 2026-11-20
Status: local

AROS ABIv1 has path-based utimes, not the descriptor setter used by
std or lutimes. Use the path helper for mtime and reject no-follow
updates rather than modifying the target of a symlink.
Verification: ABIv1 compiled and stored the expected mtime on RAM:.
The no-follow API reported Unsupported. Handle and atime semantics
are outside this patch.

--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -302,6 +302,9 @@
 where
     P: AsRef<Path>,
 {
+    #[cfg(all(target_os = "aros", target_abi = "abiv1"))]
+    return imp::set_times(p.as_ref(), None, Some(mtime), false);
+    #[cfg(not(all(target_os = "aros", target_abi = "abiv1")))]
     imp::open(p.as_ref())?.set_times(fs::FileTimes::new().set_modified(mtime.into()))
 }
 
